-- Operands of arithmetic that are not themselves arithmetic, as `l4 nlg` reads
-- them: a call, a rule's own sentence, an IF. Each #EVAL's comment is its value.
-- No two lines may read the same, and each must read with the grouping it has.

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`f2` a b MEANS a TIMES b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg %a% doubled
`dbl` a MEANS a TIMES 2

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg twice %a%
`twice` a MEANS a TIMES 2

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg %a% less %b%
`less` a b MEANS a MINUS b

#EVAL `f2` 2 5 MINUS 3                    -- 7
#EVAL `f2` 2 (5 MINUS 3)                  -- 4
#EVAL `dbl` 5 MINUS 2                     -- 8
#EVAL `dbl` (5 MINUS 2)                   -- 6
#EVAL 5 MINUS `dbl` 2                     -- 1
#EVAL `twice` 5 MINUS 2                   -- 8
#EVAL `twice` (5 MINUS 2)                 -- 6
#EVAL (IF TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 10) MINUS 3    -- -2
#EVAL IF TRUE THEN 1 ELSE (10 MINUS 3)    -- 1
#EVAL `dbl` (5 PLUS 2)                    -- 14
#EVAL 5 PLUS `dbl` 2                      -- 9
#EVAL `f2` 2 5 PLUS 3                     -- 13
#EVAL `f2` 2 (5 PLUS 3)                   -- 16
#EVAL `less` 2 (3 MINUS 5)                -- 4
#EVAL (`less` 2 3) MINUS 5                -- -6
